  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In the newer update Quest users got the ability to record videos using their camera also known as the 'Dolly' system. When you choose where the audio comes from (which is what the video picks up) you only get two options. One being 'Mic': Choosing mic means only you will be heard in the recording which is nice but what if I don't want just my voice? The second option being 'World': Choosing world means you only hear the other people mics which doesn't really make sense. I believe we should have either a third audio choice being 'All' where we can hear everyone's voices in a recording or change the meanings of the two choices we already have. Mic should mean everyone's Mic's and world should just be the world's music/ambience. Thank you for your time reading this.",
